  "findings": [
    "Locked1.12.1 captureToImage() routes Popup/multi-root to UiAutomation.takeScreenshot and crops screen bounds; ordinary Window branch uses PixelCopy with internal redraw/wait/retry behavior",
    "This implementation instead copies the actual Popup View attached Surface via public API34 builder, which SDK37 resolves using its ViewRoot native Surface and actual surfaceInsets; exact source rect recorded",
    "PixelCopy copies queued Android-rendered Surface buffers; it does not synthesize controls. One hardware frame commit is observed before requesting the copy",
    "The new capture is scoped to Popup Surface pixels; it is not whole-display occlusion/foreign-window or TalkBack proof",
    "The platform auto-allocates only the bounded requested crop; Bitmap is owned by framework until completion and by delivery/caller after callback. Errors have no success bitmap getter; no early recycle of an in-flight destination",
    "No hidden API, root registry callback override, global timeout change, input or polling retry is introduced"
  ],
